# Channel strategy

Two channels on **separate YouTube accounts**. Do not merge into one generic “AI aesthetic/ASMR” or catch-all what-if account. Keep one promise per channel.

## Channel A — After Hours Japan

- Empty night places, locked 9:16, no people/faces, soft ambient hum/drip/fridge.
- Brand = after-hours mood (Japan-first). Use `#asmr #aesthetic #liminal` in captions only — not as the channel identity.
- Series pattern: short title card (“Level B2.”) + 2–3 visual beats.
- Posting: `POSTING_SCHEDULE.md`, **21:00 IST**, `final_videos/ready/s*_hook.mp4`.

### Early analytics (mid-Sep 2026) — bias future A batches

- **Hook:** strong first-frame sensory hit (e.g. Sento ~29% stayed-to-watch).
- **Retention:** comfort + rain + food (e.g. Late Night Ramen ~83% APV).
- **Theme:** late-night food / cozy rain / warm interiors over abstract voids.

When generating A again: ECU openers, sensory titles, optional sub-15s loops.

## Channel B — Threshold Physics

- **Name / promise:** One mind-bending question → one physics **limit** → one lingering image.
- Narrow speculative physics only (no aliens-invade, no crowds/faces).
- 30–45s Shorts: VO (`guy`, slight `-rate`) + burned-in `clean` captions + `space` ambient bed.
- Art bible: photoreal cinematic CGI, void black + white-gold + cool blue→amber, locked camera.
- **Engines:** LTX-2.3 (default astro), Wan 2.2 (hard-surface stress), HunyuanVideo 1.5 (fluids/phase). **No paid video APIs.**
- Jobs: `CHANNEL=b` → `local_runner/science_prompts.py` via `run_test_batch.py`.
- **Shot modes:** `ltx_multishot` + `join_style: cut|continue` (one-pass native AV, continuous bed) preferred; `multi_cut` still available (separate clips → audio jumps).
- **Audio:** `ambient: ltx` keeps LTX score under Edge-TTS VO + `clean` captions (not synthetic `space` unless fallback).
- Posting: `POSTING_SCHEDULE_B.md`, **12:00 IST Mon–Fri**, `final_videos/ready/sci_*_hook.mp4`.
- Hashtags: `#ThresholdPhysics #space #physics #whatif #astronomy #shorts` only on B.

## Concurrent operation (Sep 2026+)

- **OK to run A and B in parallel** on cloud GPU if accounts, tags, art bibles, and batch env (`CHANNEL=a|b`) stay isolated.
- A: finish posting QC-good backlog; read analytics ~7–14 days after backlog is live.
- B: cold-start 5-episode batch; log stayed-to-watch, engaged views, APV for 14 days.

## Optional lane — Folklore / mythology micro-docs

- Deferred unless pivoting away from both A and B.

## Explicitly defer

- Cinematic history battles (faces, crowds, geography).
- Kitchen-sink “What If” (funny/action/edu mashups).

## Production defaults (both channels)

- Prefer no people / no faces / silhouettes when possible.
- Same look every post beats niche-hopping.
- Post only **QC-passed** hooks in `final_videos/ready/`.

## Generation

- Restart RunPod volume deliberately when rendering (`local_runner/render_channel_b.sh` for B).
- Channel A generation: default `CHANNEL=a` (or unset).
